"""Subject of an inverted question: the pronoun right after a question-opening auxiliary.

Component p-82af68dd@100000/layers.1.mlp.down_proj:4296 writes strongly when the token is the
subject of a question whose auxiliary or modal has been moved in front of it:
"Do I ...", "Is it ...", "Have you ...", "Am I ...", "Will we ...", "Are they ...".
It is strongest for a question that opens the sentence, somewhat weaker after a wh-word
("What do you think"), and it also fires on tag questions ("isn't it", "aren't they") and on
the inverted subjects of French ("est-ce", "a-t-il", "peut-elle") and German ("hatte ich",
"ist es"). Where the pronoun follows a noun or an ordinary verb ("the issue is that",
"to do this") it stays at zero.

