At 'respect' after 'with', recent calculus words or mathematical notation
increase the response.  Capitalized 'With' is weaker.  Additional responses
cover book editions and Mandarin comparative adverbs.  Initial whitespace,
commas, code/comment and chat markers, and auxiliary/negation words have
separate biases.  Another rule recognizes document-opening runs of spaced
periods or paired middle dots.
