C preprocessor definitions are strongest; visibility/storage modifiers and
function/class introducers give smaller positive responses. Annotations and
structured documentation have their own markers. A document-opening Title:
label also gets a strong response. Template blocks and encoding declarations
are treated as other code-header markers. The first-token "def" response is
negative, an observed positional exception. Other text is left near zero;
this intentionally omits the component's many small lexical fluctuations.
